<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>By Jeff Rueter</strong></p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The nature of international squad announce=
ments makes the final weekend before a Fifa window a precarious purgatory; =
one last chance to put in a good shift to build momentum before joining the=
 national team. Unfortunately, it=E2=80=99s also one more game that can off=
er opportunities for ill-timed knocks.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Such is life for Gio Reyna, who suffered a=
n unfortunate five-minute brace of sorts in Strasbourg=E2=80=99s match agai=
nst Toulouse on Friday. First came a goal, with Reyna navigating the French=
 mist for a one-two sequence and a clever dribble into the box past a defen=
der before powering home his shot. Then, something that=E2=80=99s happened =
far more often than goal celebrations for Reyna over the last half decade: =
an injury, thus far officially undisclosed but seemingly an issue in his le=
ft thigh.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">By Saturday=E2=80=99s end, Reyna was ruled=
 out of this month=E2=80=99s US national team camp and replaced in the squa=
d by Jack McGlynn. The Stoke City midfielder has impressed since leaving ML=
S for the English Championship, with five goals and two assists in his firs=
t 11 matches. An excellent striker of the ball, he hasn=E2=80=99t historica=
lly fared well under Mauricio Pochettino in a more withdrawn role, but he c=
ould be an intriguing alternative just beneath the striker.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">There were some good performances to singl=
e out on the eve of camp. Christian Pulisic had a man-of-the-match effort f=
or Milan, scoring the winner away at Genoa. Malik Tillman started and looke=
d the part for Bayer Leverkusen, Cavan Sullivan scored a brace on MLS Decis=
ion Day, and Mark McKenzie =E2=80=93 another camp replacement for the injur=
ed George Campbell =E2=80=93 joined Reyna among the goal scorers in Strasbo=
urg v Toulouse.</p>
